        setup: {
          players: '4 players. Each plays for herself; temporary alliances form per deal via the called King.',
          deck: '40 cards: A, K, Q, J, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2 in each suit (8s, 9s, 10s removed).',
          equipment: '40-card pack, counters or chips for stakes, score sheet.',
          dealing: '1. Dealer shuffles; pone cuts. 2. Deal 10 cards each in batches of 4-3-3, 3-4-3, or 3-3-4. 3. Deal and play rotate right (counterclockwise).',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'As Hombre (declarer), win at least six of the ten tricks, either alone (Solo) or with a partner (Alliance). Opponents aim to prevent this.',
          gameplay: '1. **Stakes**: Each player antes to the pool (or dealer antes four). 2. **Auction**: Eldest opens; players bid or pass in ascending order: Solo, Casco (with both black Aces), Dimidiator (exchange with called King), Alliance (call a King for partner). If all pass, Forced Spadille: holder of Spadille becomes Hombre and calls a King. 3. **Trump**: Hombre names trump (or partner may in Forced Spadille). 4. **Play**: Eldest leads. Must follow suit; may play any card if void. Highest trump wins, else highest of led suit. Spadille, Manille, Basta may be held back when trumps are led (unless a higher trump is led). 5. **Settlement**: Hombre wins or loses; pool and premiums paid accordingly.',
          keyRules: [
            'Spadille (Ace of Spades) is always the highest trump.',
            'Basta (Ace of Clubs) is always the third highest trump.',
            'Manille = lowest card of trump suit (2 in black suits, 7 in red suits); always second highest trump.',
            'Red suits (plain): K > Q > J > A > 2 > 3 > 4 > 5 > 6 > 7. Black suits (plain): K > Q > J > 7 > 6 > 5 > 4 > 3 > 2.',
            'Alliance: Hombre calls a non-trump King; holder is secret partner until the called card is played.',
            'Forced Spadille: No vole; Hombre and partner aim for six tricks.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Bid Alliance when you have a strong hand but need support; bid Solo when you can likely take six tricks alone. Call a King you do not hold to find a partner.',
          intermediate: "Lead to weaken opponents' trumps; use Matadors (Spadille, Manille, Basta) to control key tricks. In Alliance, signal to partner through card play.",
          advanced: 'The privilege of holding back Matadors when trumps are led allows tactical delay. Sequence your plays to maximize trump pulls. As defender, coordinate to deny Hombre a sixth trick.',
          tips: [
            'Red-suit inversion affects discard and lead choices.',
            "In Forced Spadille, the called partner's identity is secretâ€”avoid revealing through early play.",
            'Premiers bonus rewards taking six tricks before opponents take one.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
