          deckDescription: 'A stripped French deck containing 40 cards with four suits (Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, Spades) and eight ranks per suit (6, 7, 8, 9, 10, Jack, Queen, King, Ace), created by removing all 2s, 3s, 4s, and 5s from a standard 52-card deck.',
          suitDescription: 'Four traditional French suits: Hearts (Cœur), Diamonds (Carreau), Clubs (Trèfle), and Spades (Pique), each represented with standard French card iconography and color-coding for easy identification during play.',
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit in ascending order: 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, Jack (Valet), Queen (Dame), and King (Roi), with Ace as the highest card, where red suits (Hearts, Diamonds) have inverted ranking in non-trump play.',
