        prompts: {
          human: 'Four players bid for the right to be Hombre. Win the auction, name trump, and call a King to find a secret partnerâ€”or play Solo. Win six of ten tricks to take the pool. Watch out for Spadille, Manille, and Basta: the matadors that rule the trumps.',
          ai: 'Game: Quadrille. Progression: [Ante -> Deal -> Auction -> Call King -> Play(10 tricks) -> Settlement]. Bidding: Solo, Casco, Dimidiator, Alliance; or Forced Spadille if all pass. Hombre names trump; in Alliance, calls a King for partner. Matadors: Spadille (Aâ™ ), Manille (lowest trump), Basta (Aâ™£). Red suits inverted. Declarer needs 6 tricks. Follow suit. Matadors may be held back when trumps led.',
        },
        scoring: {
          description: 'Stake-based. Hombre wins: takes pool and premiums (Solo, Matadors, Premiers). Hombre loses: Remise (5 tricks) = double pool; Codille (4 or fewer) = stiffer penalty. Bonuses: Premiers (six tricks before opponents take one), Matadors (top trumps held).',
          winCondition: "Hombre (or Hombre's team) wins by taking six or more tricks. Loses with five (Remise) or four or fewer (Codille).",
          cardValues: {},
          penalties: {
            Remise: 'Hombre makes 5 tricks; loser doubles the pool.',
            Codille: 'Hombre makes 4 or fewer; opponents share pool; penalty is double Remise.',
